<file path=".tmb/diagrams/README.md">
<!-- trustmebro -->
# Diagram outline — read in this order

Updated: 2026-10-11. These are local explanatory views, not new requirements.
Source requirements retain their existing review/approval labels. Source presence
does not prove live deployment or stakeholder approval.

## 1. Use case: actors and goals

Editable source: [use-cases.puml](use-cases.puml).
Primary actor: inventory owner; draft-holder can continue identity before saving.
Personas P1/P2/P3 are behavior models, not permission roles. Goals UC-00…11
come from [catalog](../../docs/architecture/04-user-flows/use-cases.md).
Auth is a precondition for owned data, not an include arrow on every use case.
Scan is an optional assistive draft input, not autonomous stock creation.
No admin, shared-household role, push scheduler or safety verdict is invented.

## 2. UML: structure and accepted commands

- [Domain class outline](domain-class.mmd): User, FoodEntry, StockMovement,
  ApiRequest and additive Credential/Session schema relationships. Migration
  presence is not proof auth002 is applied. Attention is a derived value.
- [Component dependencies](components.mmd): active demo path is solid;
  planned UI-to-live-hook wiring is dotted. Node owns durable commands;
  Python owns transient candidates and never writes inventory.
- [Command sequence](command-sequence.mmd): authenticated owner, CSRF/key/version,
  replay before version comparison, lock/validate/update/append/save/commit,
  response and refresh. This is the backend design/source flow, not a browser
  test demonstrating the currently unwired live path.

## 3. Navigation: containers, details and overlays

Editable source: [navigation.mmd](navigation.mmd).
Solid edges map App/Shell local state; dotted edges mark live auth/scan/routes
that are not entry-reachable. Parent breadcrumb is the current collection
container (inventory or attention), not a stack of every visited screen.
Current food name remains the detail h1; top-level lists need no breadcrumb.
Rare direct-entry/create from settings/trash retains that View's parent label
because the existing return callback goes there; no unrelated routing rule changed.
Create/edit/action/history stay overlays, not invented URL routes.
Canonical candidate live routes remain [DOC-NAV](../../docs/architecture/05-interaction-design/navigation.md).

## Evidence and maintenance

Read [web layout](../layouts/web/LAYOUT.md), [API layout](../layouts/api/LAYOUT.md),
[DB layout](../layouts/database/LAYOUT.md), [task specs](../tasks/README.md).
Schema source: [001](../../database/mysql/migrations/001_initial_schema.sql),
[002](../../database/mysql/migrations/002_local_auth.sql).
Do not draw a new entity because a UI card exists. Change a diagram together with
its source map and root task; keep proposed and active edges distinguishable.
</file>

