P1 reported sidebar white text on white background1.00:1 at1024/1280/1440/1920.
Disposition: the1.00:1 value does not represent the actual blue gradient;
the probe's computed-color sampling does not evaluate background-image endpoints.
Source index.css defines normal gradient #075fad→#0d75db and hover
#0a6dd6→#1084f2. Relative-luminance calculation gives white contrast normal
6.46/4.58 and hover5.03/3.75. Therefore the normal-state report is a measurement
limitation, while existing hover-state small-text contrast is a real remaining risk.
UX-01 scopes review and source-owned correction; it is not marked fixed.

Other retained observations: existing movement borders change on hover;
edit/delete/history/skip link focus consistency warnings; movement focus rings;
intentionally centered wide content at1920. These are outside breadcrumb source
changes. Do not remove keyboard feedback to make a taste heuristic quiet.
