# App layout — composition across web, API, scan and persistence

Updated: 2026-10-11. “App” means system composition; “web” means its current
React frontend. No native mobile application/package exists in the inspected tree.
Status view: [ROADMAP](ROADMAP.md). Diagram: [components](../../diagrams/components.mmd).

| Boundary | Entrypoint | State/effect owner | Detail |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Web presentation | `apps/web/src/main.tsx` | App view/filter/modal/draft; current mock memory | [web](../web/LAYOUT.md) |
| Remote UI coordinator | `apps/web/src/hooks/useExpiry.ts` | identity epoch, async data and retained command; not mounted | [contracts](../contracts/LAYOUT.md) |
| Public HTTP app | `apps/api/src/app.mjs` | composition, trusted identity/CSRF, modules | [API](../api/LAYOUT.md) |
| Authoritative inventory | `apps/api/src/shared/repository.mjs` | transaction/replay/version/history with pure domain rules | [DB](../database/LAYOUT.md) |
| Scan gateway | `apps/api/src/modules/scan/scan.service.mjs` | bounded remote OCR call, response validation, no inventory write | [scan](../scan/LAYOUT.md) |
| Python service | `services/python-scan/app/main.py` | image/OCR/parser candidate extraction only | [scan](../scan/LAYOUT.md) |
| Durable store | `database/mysql/migrations/001_initial_schema.sql` | physical schema and constraints; runner owns migration ledger | [DB](../database/LAYOUT.md) |
| Public/internal contracts | `contracts/public-api.yaml`, `contracts/scan-api.yaml` | vocabulary/schema; adapter maps UI-friendly types | [contracts](../contracts/LAYOUT.md) |
| Startup/deployment | `compose.yaml`, `vercel.json` | container/proxy/build configuration, not feature acceptance | [delivery](../delivery/LAYOUT.md) |
| Documentation | `docs/README.md` | provenance/design/review records, not live behavior | [docs](../docs/LAYOUT.md) |

## Dependency and lifecycle contracts

Current web: boot, mock list, selected detail, user form callback, synchronous
mock commit, revision recompute, notice. Closing a form does not mutate inventory.
Future live slice: session principal, owner-epoch query, controlled UI, frozen
command, HTTP auth/CSRF/key, transaction, original public DTO, accepted refresh.
UI cannot establish trusted owner or override domain rules.

New feature must choose its owner before adding components: UI-only means no
API/table; read projection means no ledger event; accepted physical action means
versioned atomic command; assistive scan means candidate review before creation.

## Reuse and feature navigation

Use existing controlled forms/primitives; compose variants instead of cloning
screens. Shared kernel extraction is TMB::F-05, not assumed safe merely because
files are identical. Connection adapters retain lifecycle ownership.
Each task SPEC names triggers, affected UI navigation, APIs/contracts, table/rule
impact, ordered implementation steps and actual acceptance gates.
Start at [task index](../../tasks/README.md) and [feature-impact](../../maps/feature-impact.md).
