# Contracts, types, projections and mapping boundaries

Updated: 2026-10-11. [A] Inspected current source; `.tmb/layouts/contracts/ROADMAP.md`.

## Contract and adapter owners

| Source | Responsibility | Consumers / effect |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `contracts/public-api.yaml` | OpenAPI3.1.1,13 core +4 auth operations, session cookie schemes, Entry/Movement/Preferences/Problem | public DTO owner and consumer checks |
| `contracts/openapi.json` | JSON contract snapshot with current matching path/auth inventory | API schema tests; not runtime router registration |
| `contracts/scan-api.yaml` | internal health/scan operation/schema | Node↔Python boundary |
| `contracts/schema_reference_mysql.sql` | reference core SQL | migration001 is application source authority |
| `contracts/fixtures.json` | contract examples | fixtures, not production data |
| `apps/api/src/shared/public-dto.mjs` | Entry/lifecycle/attention, signed movement delta, UTC timestamp and preferences projection | shared HTTP-facing mapping |
| `apps/api/src/modules/inventory/public-inventory.repository.mjs` | public snapshot before result cache commit | replay preserves original DTO/as-of date |
| `apps/api/src/shared/middleware.mjs` | sanitized public problem serialization | API failures |
| `apps/api/src/modules/scan/scan.service.mjs` | publicScanResult structural validation and confirmation projection | public scan response |
| `services/python-scan/app/schemas/scan.py` | internal Pydantic response | Python scan/health routes |
| `apps/web/src/domain/types.ts` | UI-friendly type view | presentation components |
| `apps/web/src/api/client.ts` | fromEntry/fromMovement, draftDTO/createDTO, decimal, immutable Command, ApiError, request | useExpiry and future App integration |
| `apps/web/src/mockApi.ts` | separate demo shape, fake IDs, numeric quantities and fixed date | current running UI |

## Explicit vocabulary/shape translation

| Meaning | API / DB | UI | Translation owner |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Quantity | decimal string; exact milliunit arithmetic | number for input/display | client decimal/fromEntry; domain milli/decimal |
| Date certainty | known / estimated / unknown | exact / estimated / unknown | client draftDTO/fromEntry |
| Date source | printed_label / user_entered / user_estimate / unknown | package_label / user_reentered / user_estimate / null | client mapper |
| Date label | use_by / best_before / unspecified | use_by / best_before / unknown | client mapper |
| Attention | past_date / due_today / soon / unknown / later / inactive | past / today / soon / unknown / later / undefined | client attentionMap; backend is authority |
| Quantity correction kind | adjustment | recount | fromMovement; feature action names remain recount |
| Deleted visibility | UTC deleted_at, separate from remaining quantity | trash versus list | domain/repository and App view |
| Public errors | Problem requires type/title/status/code | ApiClient reads body.code | middleware currently omits code; F-06 |
| Missing location | omitted → unspecified in domain; supplied null rejected | EntryForm emits null when empty | draftDTO currently forwards null; F-06 |
| Scan candidates | nested object fields food_name/expiry_date/manufactured_date | client/ScanForm expect candidate[] | F-02 pending explicit adapter |
| Session principal | durable hashed-token cookie lookup | hook session.user with owner epoch | createAuthBoundary + useExpiry; not wired to App |

## Adding/changing a field [D]

1. Establish requirement/grain/validation/null/default/unit and whether it persists.
2. Update a forward migration only when durable schema changes are necessary.
3. Update authoritative domain normalization + repository transaction + public DTO.
4. Update OpenAPI schema/examples and deliberately regenerate/reconcile JSON snapshot.
5. Update UI types and the existing transport mapper; preserve UI-friendly vocabulary.
6. Compose the field inside EntryForm or a relevant feature, reusing Field/controls.
7. Check omitted/null/known/unknown, stale version, replay before/after preference/time
   changes, ownership and error code mapping. Record requirement namespace explicitly.

## Constraints and verification

Caller-provided identity never establishes the principal. Exact decimal arithmetic
belongs to backend; component previews are UX checks. Derived attention remains out
of schema. The API facade must not recompute a replay's snapshot after current state
changes. `apps/api/tests/public-contract.test.mjs` validates injected success projections;
passing it does not cover all error outputs/scan/client mappings.
Fresh requirement IDs retain SYS-/FINAL CHECK/design namespaces. Relevant tracked
registries: `docs/architecture/11-traceability/id-register.md`,
`docs/architecture/11-traceability/registry.json`.
</file>

