# Database layout, tables, rules and migration lifecycle

Updated: 2026-10-11. [A] Definition map; no live DDL executed for this task.
Status view: `.tmb/layouts/database/ROADMAP.md`.

## Schema owners

| Source | Responsibility | Evidence boundary |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `database/mysql/migrations/001_initial_schema.sql` | four core InnoDB tables, indexes/FKs/CHECK/generated helper | current source-defined physical schema |
| `database/mysql/migrations/002_local_auth.sql` | additive credential/session definitions | file header retains proposal/approval comment; not proof applied |
| `database/mysql/src/connection.mjs` | restricted sandbox connection/admin commands; migrate001/grants/checksum | migrate creates schema_migrations; rejects partial unversioned schema |
| `database/mysql/scripts/auth-migration.mjs` | explicitly selected002 executor/advisory lock/snapshots/checksum/grants | must be invoked for actual application; not invoked here |
| `database/mysql/scripts/manage.mjs` | migrate/verify/dump/seed tooling | can mutate data/evidence; commands not part of map generation |
| `database/mysql/scripts/init-env.mjs` | generated private development credentials | existing env remains private; not copied to maps |
| `database/mysql/seed.sql` | deterministic fixture owners/entries/events | demo test data, not user data |
| `database/mysql/src/domain.mjs` | sandbox pure inventory rules | byte-identical API domain; tracked duplicate |
| `database/mysql/src/repository.mjs` | sandbox command/ledger/replay tests | byte-identical API repository; different connection adapter |
| `apps/api/src/shared/connection.mjs` | runtime pool/environment/UTC setup | app runtime; no automatic migration |
| `database/mysql/compose.yaml` | dedicated loopback MySQL development sandbox | isolated volume/project from root Compose |
| `database/mysql/workbench_export.py` | native GRT/export parity evidence | saved evidence is historical; not current SQL introspection |
| `database/mysql/workbench_open.py`, `database/mysql/workbench_show_model.py` | graphical model/open verification | requires native Workbench/session |
| `database/mysql/tests/run.mjs` | fresh isolated DB business/concurrency/rollback/restore tests | DB-creating test; not run here |
| `database/mysql/tests/static.mjs` | saved source/ERD evidence checks | some historical doc paths may drift |

## Complete table responsibilities and fields

| Table | Fields | Relations / role |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| users | id, identity_subject, display_name, timezone, attention_lead_days, version, created_at, updated_at | owner entity; unique identity_subject; mutable versioned prefs |
| food_entries | id, user_id, name, storage_location, remaining_quantity, unit, expiry_date, date_certainty, date_source, date_label_type, opened_on, note, version, deleted_at, created_at, updated_at | many entries/user; owner FK RESTRICT; remaining DECIMAL(12,3); independent visibility and quantity lifecycle |
| stock_movements | id, entry_id, kind, quantity_before, quantity_after, reason, recorded_at, generated initial_entry_id | many events/entry; unique generated initial helper; immutable through ordinary app path |
| api_requests | user_id, idempotency_key, operation, request_hash, response_status, response_body, created_at | composite owner+key PK; stable replay snapshot/status/hash |
| local_credentials | user_id, email_normalized, password_verifier, created_at, updated_at | one credential row/user; unique normalized email; no plaintext password |
| user_sessions | token_hash, user_id, created_at, last_seen_at, expires_at, revoked_at | many sessions/user; only token hash; expiry/revocation/owner indexes |
| schema_migrations | version, sha256, applied_at | runner-created ledger, no user FK |

Six CREATE TABLE declarations in migrations + one runner-created schema_migrations.
Migrations override schema reference snapshots when they disagree. References:
`contracts/schema_reference_mysql.sql`; saved model/extract under
`docs/architecture/06-data-model/erd-workbench/` (folder reference, no live claim).

## Integrity and state authority

| Rule | DB enforcement | Service/transaction enforcement |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Quantity positive create, nonnegative remaining | decimal quantity≥0; whole piece CHECK | milli/positive create; stock movement coupled to current quantity |
| Date/source/certainty coherence | CHECK allowed enum + coherent null/known/estimated | metadata normalizes and validates calendar values |
| Owner isolation | user FKs | every public command/read uses trusted owner; lock/read owner filters |
| Initial event | unique generated initial_entry_id | create inserts initial child in same transaction; FK cannot force minimum child |
| Ledger consistency | row shape checks | exact milliunit calculation, append+quantity update together |
| Concurrent writes | version≥1 CHECK | FOR UPDATE + expected_version; no stale overwrite |
| Retry dedup | owner/key PK; status/body pair CHECK | operation+fingerprint and saved original DTO before commit |
| Delete versus discard | deleted_at and movement kind are separate | soft-delete/restore affect visibility; discard affects physical quantity |
| Attention | no attention column | runtime owner timezone/clock/lead rule recomputed; UI displays result |
| Credential/session lifecycle | unique email/hash, FK, timestamps | verify password, rotate/revoke, enforce idle+absolute expiry |

## Changing persistent state [D]

Map entity/grain/invariants first; add a new forward migration, never rewrite applied001.
Trace schema → repository/domain → public DTO/schema → client UI mapping → user action.
Review fresh install and upgrades, grants/indexes/backups and partial DDL recovery.
MySQL DDL auto-commits; failure preservation is distinct from transaction rollback.
Prefer domain-only or read projection changes when no new durable state is needed.
Do not persist attention or scan candidates solely because a screen displays them.

F-05 owns proposed shared kernel extraction; F-06 owns migration/Compose lifecycle review.
</file>

