# Documentation layout — source, design, implementation, verification

Updated: 2026-10-11. Entry: [docs README](../../../docs/README.md).
Current repo paths win over stale paths printed inside older authored documents.
Catalog and link diagnostics are generated by `python3 .tmb/tools/knowledge.py catalog`.
Status: [.tmb docs roadmap](ROADMAP.md); per-folder detail: [catalog](CATALOG.md).

## Reading order and responsibilities

| Order / folder | What it owns | Read for | Downstream |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 00-context | definition, scope, sources, glossary, owner/decision ledgers | purpose and evidence boundaries; distinguish definition from delivery scope | requirements and ADRs |
| 01-personas | P01/P02/P03, persona gaps, FINAL CHECK crosswalk | actual need and source namespace; personas are not roles | food use cases and acceptance tasks |
| 02-challenges | research, food-date semantics, OCR studies | evidence/constraints, not implementation proof | scope, candidate handling and uncertainty |
| 03-requirements-features | business/stakeholder/system/NFR, rules, feature catalog | named behavior, immutable rules and measurable acceptance | UC/flows, DTOs, task specs |
| 04-user-flows | UC-00…11, scenarios, UF, PlantUML | actor goals, preconditions, success/error guarantees | screen state and API commands |
| 05-interaction-design | navigation, wireframes, screen states, sequences | transitions, overlays, error/back/draft contracts | web composition and tests |
| 06-data-model | grain, fields, entities, ERD, Workbench evidence | logical design; saved evidence is historical | migrations and repositories |
| 07-api | endpoints, protocol, auth and scan contract narrative | intended transport and errors | contracts and public projections |
| 08-architecture | ADR-001…006, component/deploy/observability design | chosen boundaries and proposal changes | apps/services/database and delivery |
| 09-advanced-web | historical layout, state integration, extension process | intended UI owner model; reconcile old paths with current web layout | client/hook/App |
| 10-testing | cases, coverage, dated source audits and reports | acceptance identity and evidence limits | verification gates |
| 11-traceability | registry/id-register/tracking/hashes | graph references, not automatic approval | feature specs and audits |
| 12-process | workstreams/gates/task tracker/TMB copies | process/reference examples, not active runtime | root PLAN/ROADMAP |
| consolidated | native-source snapshots and historical extraction/PDF | provenance; do not promote raw snapshots to current rules | source register/crosswalk |
| tooling | validators and saved metadata | structural diagnostics, not product correctness | local review |

## Specific source entrypoints

- System: [definition](../../../docs/architecture/00-context/system-definition.md),
  [scope](../../../docs/architecture/00-context/scope.md),
  [requirements summary](../../../docs/architecture/03-requirements-features/Expiry_System_Requirements_Summary.md).
- Food design: [functional requirements](../../../docs/architecture/03-requirements-features/system-requirements.md),
  [business rules](../../../docs/architecture/03-requirements-features/business-rules.md),
  [features](../../../docs/architecture/03-requirements-features/features.md),
  [use cases](../../../docs/architecture/04-user-flows/use-cases.md).
- UI: [navigation](../../../docs/architecture/05-interaction-design/navigation.md),
  [screen states](../../../docs/architecture/05-interaction-design/screen-state-matrix.md).
- Traceability: [crosswalk](../../../docs/architecture/01-personas/final-check-persona-alignment.md),
  [registry](../../../docs/architecture/11-traceability/registry.json).
- Runtime reality: [app](../app/LAYOUT.md), [web](../web/LAYOUT.md),
  [API](../api/LAYOUT.md), [DB](../database/LAYOUT.md), [contracts](../contracts/LAYOUT.md).

## Namespaces — never join by bare numeric ID

`food::F-01` means manual capture in the design catalog; `TMB::F-01` means live
integration backlog. They are not the same task. Food FR-03 is attention;
FINAL CHECK::FR-03 is metadata/amount/location update; SYS-FR-03 is accepted events.
SYS requirements are whole-system synthesis. FINAL CHECK is a source snapshot;
food design is a specific proposal. Crosswalk relationships are semantic support,
not automatic equivalence or approval. Local specs use CAP-01…08 to avoid collision.

## Reorder and authority

The existing numbered docs already separate concerns. Local linked entrypoints
reorder reading, not tracked originals. No physical doc/source move in this batch.
See [reorder receipt](../../09_AUDIT/BATCH_1_LINKED_REORDER.md).
Broken links in source docs remain visible in `.tmb/evidence/docs-link-audit.json`.
DOC-01 proposes a reference-only repair batch;
it must verify target meaning rather than revive obsolete directory aliases.

Search returns evidence snippets with file/heading/line/hash/status. Read the cited
source before changing rules; a generated catalog is never a second rule owner.
</file>

