# Scan service layout and confirmation boundary

Updated: 2026-10-11. [A] Current source; `.tmb/layouts/scan/ROADMAP.md` links root tasks.

## Components and dependencies

| Source | Symbol / responsibility | Consumers |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `services/python-scan/app/main.py` | FastAPI app, ScanError JSON handler and router mounts | Uvicorn |
| `services/python-scan/app/routes/scan.py` | scan_image bounds body; process_scan; extract_ocr_text; tesseract_available | POST /scan; health capability |
| `services/python-scan/app/routes/health.py` | get_health | GET /health; reports actual Tesseract availability |
| `services/python-scan/app/schemas/scan.py` | ScanError, HealthResponse, ExpiryCandidate, ManufacturedCandidate, Candidates, ScanResult | route/parser/output schema |
| `services/python-scan/app/scanner/preprocessor.py` | decode_image_bytes, preprocess_image; EXIF transpose/grayscale/autocontrast; codec/dimension guards | scan processing |
| `services/python-scan/app/scanner/date_parser.py` | classify_label_type, label_before_date, parse_date_candidates, normalized_candidates | post-OCR candidate interpretation |
| `services/python-scan/requirements.txt` | FastAPI/Uvicorn/Pydantic/multipart/Pillow/pytesseract | Python environment |
| `services/python-scan/Dockerfile` | Python3.12 + Tesseract/eng/vie binaries, Uvicorn | root Compose |
| `services/python-scan/tests/test_scanner.py` | classifier/parser/base64/preprocess unit cases | existing unittest suite |
| `apps/api/src/modules/scan/scan.upload.mjs` | validates public upload and base64/signature/size | Node ScanController |
| `apps/api/src/modules/scan/scan.service.mjs` | deadline + internal fetch + publicScanResult projection | Node scan router |
| `apps/web/src/features/ScanForm.tsx` | file state/result/review draft | current inactive component; expects candidates array |

## Endpoints and data flow

| Method/path | Input | Output / boundary |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| GET /health | none | health/service/version/tesseract_available; capability readiness |
| POST /scan | JSON image_base64 or multipart file | object candidates.food_name/expiry_date/manufactured_date, raw_text, warnings/errors, duration |

Node `/api/v1/scans` accepts multipart `image`; legacy `/api/v1/scan` uses `file`.
Node sends JSON base64 to Python. Python rejects body/codec/base64 errors, preprocesses
in memory, runs OCR in threadpool with2.5-second OCR timeout; Node total request
deadline defaults3 seconds. Candidate regex interpretations preserve source_text,
ambiguity alternatives and requires_confirmation. Manufactured dates are separate;
unlabelled dates do not gain expiry meaning. No scan component writes inventory.

`upload → bounded decode → Pillow validation/preprocess → Tesseract → labelled
date parser → candidates → Node response projection → user review/edit → separate
inventory create`. The final frontend review/save chain remains unconnected.

## Reuse and feature wiring

Reuse decode/processor/parser and Pydantic candidate shape. Route adapters perform
transport-specific checks; domain date meaning stays in the parser. Public confirmation
guard stays in Node projection and review workflow. Reuse EntryForm for final correction;
explicit create is the only point where MySQL should receive confirmed data.

F-02: client `ScanResult.candidates` and ScanForm use an array but Node projection
returns a nested object. Define one tested transport adapter before exposing a scan CTA.
F-06: test_preprocess_empty_image expects tuple/error text while processor raises ScanError;
this is a source-observed test mismatch, not an executed failure under the missing environment.
Current Python test command fails at pydantic import; see `.tmb/VERIFICATION.md`.
</file>

