# Web layout and ownership

Updated: 2026-10-11. [A] Static entry/import evidence, current develop checkout.
Status projection: `.tmb/layouts/web/ROADMAP.md`; task truth: root `ROADMAP.md`.

## Runtime and directory responsibilities

| Path | Responsibility / state owner | Dependencies / consumers |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `apps/web/index.html` | root mount and module boot | main.tsx; Vite site config |
| `apps/web/src/main.tsx` | React StrictMode boot and scrollbar lifecycle | App, CSS, ScrollbarAutohide |
| `apps/web/src/App.tsx` | started/auth simulation, view, filters, selectedId, actionEntryId, modal, draft, notices/revision | feature components, mock singleton |
| `apps/web/src/demo/DemoApp.tsx` | App clone, relative imports changed; now424lines | currently not imported by entry |
| `apps/web/src/mockApi.ts` | demo user/data/ledger/key cache/date policy and fixed clock | current App; no network or durable DB |
| `apps/web/src/domain/types.ts` | UI shape; canonical DTO is mapped by client | screens/format; no exported DEMO_DATE |
| `apps/web/src/lib/format.ts` | date/quantity/time/VI labels and attention guidance | Badge/detail/list/history/forms |
| `apps/web/src/components/layout/Shell.tsx` | View union and desktop/mobile navigation; presentation callbacks | App; Icon |
| `apps/web/src/components/layout/Grid.tsx` | grid wrapper | Detail/Inventory/Trash/Settings |
| `apps/web/src/components/layout/PageHeader.tsx` | page title/actions | Inventory/Trash/Settings |
| `apps/web/src/components/layout/Breadcrumb.tsx` | controlled collection-parent callbacks, named nav/list, nearest parent at narrow widths | Detail; existing Icon and CSS tokens; no router/fetch/state |
| `apps/web/src/components/ui/Button.tsx` | variants/loading/icon/disabled/button semantics | screens, forms, dialogs |
| `apps/web/src/components/ui/Modal.tsx` | dialog surface, focus/escape/scroll lifecycle; ModalActions footer | all modal forms/history/dialogs |
| `apps/web/src/components/ui/Field.tsx` | label/hint/error/fieldset presentation | entry/movement/settings/auth |
| `apps/web/src/components/ui/DatePicker.tsx` | controlled ISO date picker, calendar/keyboard/portal state | EntryForm |
| `apps/web/src/components/ui/Select.tsx` | controlled generic options, search/highlight/keyboard/portal state | EntryForm/Inventory/Settings |
| `apps/web/src/components/ui/Segmented.tsx` | controlled typed choice buttons | EntryForm |
| `apps/web/src/components/ui/Badge.tsx` | attention label+icon rendering | FoodCard/Detail; domain types+format |
| `apps/web/src/components/ui/Card.tsx` | generic surface | Detail/Settings/Trash |
| `apps/web/src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx` | title/body/actions | Inventory/Trash |
| `apps/web/src/components/ui/Icon.tsx` | SVG name registry | primitive and feature consumers |
| `apps/web/src/components/ui/ScrollbarAutohide.tsx` | global scroll affordance/event cleanup | main |
| `apps/web/src/index.css` | tokens/layout/desktop-mobile responsive styles | app plus all component class contracts |
| `apps/web/src/api/client.ts` | cookie/CSRF requests, DTO translation, stable commands and retry | useExpiry/ScanForm source only |
| `apps/web/src/hooks/useExpiry.ts` | session identity epoch, async list/detail/history, pending immutable command, same-command retry | not used by current App |

## Feature component inventory

| Feature | Inputs / output | Responsibility / reuse |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `apps/web/src/features/Welcome.tsx` | onStart/onDemo | onboarding actions; no auth backend |
| `apps/web/src/features/Inventory.tsx` | mode, data, counts, filters, attention, action callbacks | one list for attention/inventory variants; asOfDate/demo props exist |
| `apps/web/src/features/FoodCard.tsx` | food, attention, onOpen/onAction | one reusable food row and action entry |
| `apps/web/src/features/Detail.tsx` | food, attention, movements, timezone, onBack/onAction/parentLabel | projection/actions and one parent breadcrumb; no mutation authority |
| `apps/web/src/features/EntryForm.tsx` | entry? / initial? / initialStep; onCreate/onUpdate | one create/edit/date form; draft state owned inside; optional date step |
| `apps/web/src/features/MovementForm.tsx` | food + mode consume/discard/recount; onSave | one quantity form; mode copy config; user preview/validation |
| `apps/web/src/features/History.tsx` | food, movements, onClose | history dialog, no ledger edits |
| `apps/web/src/features/Trash.tsx` | foods/onRestore | deleted-item list; restore callback |
| `apps/web/src/features/Settings.tsx` | prefs/displayName/onSave | preference draft and controls |
| `apps/web/src/features/StatusDialog.tsx` | StatusMode/onClose; exported Dialog config | recovery/confirmation presentation reused by delete/restore/auth simulation |
| `apps/web/src/features/AuthForm.tsx` | pending/error, async onSubmit, onClose | login/register field state; not reached |
| `apps/web/src/features/ScanForm.tsx` | async onScan, onReview draft, onClose | upload/review surface; not reached; expects array candidates |

## State and feedback

`Shell callback → App.navigate → view/reset IDs/filters → selected Detail or selected view`.
`EntryForm/MovementForm callback → App.commit → mock command → revision → memo reads → notice`.
For a future live feature: App controls UI/draft; useExpiry controls remote session/data/
pending request; ApiClient controls transport/mapping; backend controls business state.
An API failure must not silently select demo state.

## Change boundaries

New top-level view: View union, desktop sidebar metadata, mobile dock, App initialization
allowlist/render/navigate, CSS and context/navigation map. Detail/modal-only action needs
DetailAction or ModalKind/form dispatch, list and detail entrypoints and close/return behavior.
Reusable primitives receive data/callbacks; no primitive owns session, fetch, SQL or domain writes.
See `.tmb/maps/navigation.md` and `.tmb/maps/reuse.md`.

## Gaps / checks

F-00 closed during responsive work: unused DEMO_DATE import removed; attention callback
accepts Pick<FoodEntry, expiry_date>, matching the actual policy input. Typing/build pass.
F-01: current App has no useExpiry/AuthForm/ScanForm import. F-03: exact App/DemoApp body clone.
F-04: queries initialize once; no history synchronization. Tests/build baseline is recorded in
`.tmb/VERIFICATION.md`; responsive checks are detailed below, not live acceptance.

NAV-01 replaces Detail's back presentation with a shared breadcrumb. Both App and
DemoApp pass current View's exact parent label. The callback still only clears
selection, preserving filters and originating container. No breadcrumb is added
to top-level pages or modal steps. NAV-01 does not implement F-04 URL semantics.
Specific specs: `.tmb/tasks/README.md`; docs context: `.tmb/layouts/docs/LAYOUT.md`.

## RSP-01…07 responsive ownership and acceptance

Contract and source receipt: `.tmb/responsive/PLAN.md`; executable gates:
`.tmb/responsive/GATES.md`; evidence: `.tmb/evidence/responsive/pages.json`.

- CSS owns one relative type scale,16px default body/mobile explanatory copy,
  diacritic-safe wrapping, visible keyboard focus and44px mobile action height.
  Dense seven-column calendar uses24px minimum measured targets, not a claim
  that every calendar cell is44px wide at320px.
- Grid is4/8/12 columns at768/1024px. Inventory uses content-fit cards (minimum
  320px or available width); Detail remains one column until1280px, then7/5.
  Large quantity sits below the name at every width; no global overflow masking.
- Shell uses dynamic viewport height, content/scroll clearance for fixed dock
  and safe-area padding. Mobile footer aligns two actions or two+full-width CTA;
  short landscape reduces chrome padding, not body text or available actions.
- Modal still owns focus trap/restoration/scroll lock; CSS owns contained body,
  bounded header and footer. DatePicker/Select own visualViewport positioning
  and listener cleanup. Calendar has viewport-bounded internal scroll and keeps
  keyboard-selected cells in view; ISO date and controlled option callbacks remain.
- Browser matrix covers current pages/empty/filter/stress states, dialogs and
  render-only AuthForm/ScanForm harnesses. These harnesses do not wire live auth/OCR.
  Enlarged CSS text200%, keyboard, reduced-motion and compiled-preview checks
  are local Chromium evidence; actual Safari/iPhone/keyboard/screen reader is untested.
