<file path=".tmb/maps/flows.md">
<!-- trustmebro -->
# Cross-component flows, owners and feedback

Updated: 2026-10-11. Solid flows below are implemented source chains; dashed web
integration links are [D] future wiring. Backend routes exist independently of UI.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  Boot[main.tsx] --> App[App UI state]
  App --> UI[Shell and feature components]
  App --> Mock[mockApi in memory]
  Mock --> Revision[revision / notice]
  Revision --> App
  UI -. future callbacks .-> Hook[useExpiry]
  Hook -. future live entry .-> Client[ApiClient]
  Client -. future browser requests .-> Boundary[Express session / CSRF / key]
  Boundary --> Service[feature services]
  Service --> Repo[transaction repository]
  Repo --> DB[(MySQL)]
  Repo --> DTO[public DTO before replay cache]
  DTO --> Response[HTTP response]
  Service --> Scan[Python scan]
  Scan --> Candidate[candidate object / confirmation]
```

## Full feature slices

| Slice | Input → process → state → event → effect → output → feedback |
| :--- | :--- |
| Current create | Welcome/Shell/Inventory add → EntryForm draft → App pendingCreate/auth simulation → mock create key → fake entry+initial history → selected detail/notice → memo reload via revision |
| Backend create | confirmed metadata/decimal/unit → auth/CSRF/key → InventoryService/PublicInventoryRepository → reservation+entry+initial append in one transaction → saved public Entry →201/Location → [D] client selects/refreshes |
| Use/discard | FoodCard/Detail action → MovementForm mode/amount/reason preview → App commit/mock in current UI; backend repo.mutate with owner/key/version → quantity decrement+immutable event → MutationResult/replay → [D] refresh list/detail/history/counts |
| Recount | actual physical quantity+reason → same form mode recount → repository lock/version/milli → adjustment only if changed → no-op200 or changed201 → [D] updated quantity/history and attention |
| Date correction | date action → EntryForm step1 → metadata normalization → edit transaction/version → Entry with current projection → [D] attention recomputed and list reclassified |
| Delete/restore | Detail delete/Trash restore confirmation → soft visibility command → deleted_at/version only → list/trash membership changes; ledger remains →204/Entry → reset selection/return inventory |
| Preferences | Settings draft → versioned prefs command → owner row lock/timezone+lead update → derived attention changes on next read → Preferences → [D] refresh counts and display owner-local as_of |
| Login/session | AuthForm future callback → ApiClient auth/session → crypto+AuthRepository → salted verifier/hash-only session → cookie and CSRF → hook accepts owner, changes epoch → owner-bound data/draft reset policy |
| Scan | upload → Node bounded validation → Python Pillow/OCR/parser → transient candidates only → nested result with confirmation → [D] mapper/review EntryForm → explicit create command → persistent inventory |
| Retry/uncertain result | future immutable newCommand → ApiClient retries same serialized body/key → hook retains pending on uncertain failure → repo finds owner/key/hash saved result before version → exact original response → clear pending/refresh; new command cannot silently replace unresolved one |

## Ownership rules across slices

- UI draft/navigation: App and feature form state; canceled input is not a DB event.
- Remote session/query/pending command: useExpiry; ignore prior-owner in-flight results.
- HTTP shape/decimal/enum translation: ApiClient/public-dto; no generic widget fetch.
- Domain meaning: backend domain rules and command service/repository.
- Durable quantities/history/replay: one MySQL command transaction.
- Scan interpretation: parser preserves source and uncertainty; user confirms record.
- Delivery: composition/config; no service entry is a universal state controller.

Dependencies point from UI to adapter and HTTP to service/domain/repository; Python
does not import inventory SQL. Broad adapter consolidation must preserve pool versus
sandbox lifecycle and pre-cache DTO mapping. Source details are in the six layouts.
</file>

<file path=".tmb/maps/navigation.md">
<!-- trustmebro -->
# Navigation, screens and actions

Updated: 2026-10-11. [A] `apps/web/src/App.tsx` and
`apps/web/src/components/layout/Shell.tsx` own the current navigation.
All rows describe current source unless [D] marked. There are no pathname routes.
`window.location.search` is read once. `view`, `selectedId` and `modal` then control
navigation; state changes do not call pushState or register popstate.

## Screens and selection precedence

| Entry / state | Render owner | Transition / return | API destination when integrated |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `/` without demo/started | `apps/web/src/features/Welcome.tsx` | onStart sets started/add; onDemo sets started/authenticated | [D] verified session or explicit demo |
| `?demo` or `?started` | App started initializer | presence flag; demo also authenticates simulation | [D] do not use as trusted principal |
| `view=attention` (default) | `apps/web/src/features/Inventory.tsx` mode attention | filters out later/depleted; shows unknown | GET food-entries view=attention |
| `view=inventory` | Inventory mode inventory | shared filter/list view | GET food-entries view=inventory |
| `view=trash` | `apps/web/src/features/Trash.tsx` | onRestore selects deleted record + restore modal | GET trash/food-entries |
| `view=settings` | `apps/web/src/features/Settings.tsx` | onSave commits; same view retained | GET/PATCH me/preferences |
| selected nondeleted id (`?id` initial or row callback) | `apps/web/src/features/Detail.tsx` | takes precedence over view; onBack clears selection | GET food-entries/{id} |
| detail parent breadcrumb | `apps/web/src/components/layout/Breadcrumb.tsx` | current container label from App/DemoApp; same onBack clears selection without resetting filters | display-only; no HTTP |
| selected deleted id | App avoids Detail branch | trash remains visible; confirmation uses selected | restore command |
| sidebar / brand / mobile dock | Shell callback to App.navigate | clears selectedId/actionEntryId; resets list filters for inventory/attention | [D] selected view query reload |

`?view=` allows inventory/attention/trash/settings; invalid value falls back to attention.
`?modal=` is currently cast without validating enum; unsupported values render nothing.

## Every action/modal mode

| Action | Entry points | Owner / variant | Result and return |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| add | Shell desktop add/mobile center, Inventory empty/header, Welcome start | `apps/web/src/features/EntryForm.tsx` create | callback create; pending draft if unauthenticated; selects created record after success |
| edit | Detail/edit action | EntryForm entry+initialStep0 | mock update metadata; close/refresh; quantity/unit read-only |
| date | FoodCard/Detail/check-date action | EntryForm entry+initialStep1 | date correction; same selected record or list |
| consume | FoodCard quick action, Detail | `apps/web/src/features/MovementForm.tsx` mode consume | decrement quantity; history appended; modal closes |
| discard | FoodCard/Detail | MovementForm mode discard | separate physical disposal history; modal closes |
| recount | FoodCard/Detail including depleted recovery | MovementForm mode recount | actual quantity, reason required; no-op blocked in UI |
| history | Detail | `apps/web/src/features/History.tsx` | current mock movement list; close returns detail |
| delete | Detail | exported Dialog in `apps/web/src/features/StatusDialog.tsx` | soft-delete; success clears selection |
| restore | Trash onRestore | same Dialog | mock restore; success navigate inventory, clear selection/filter |
| authPending | unauthenticated create | App's demo-only Dialog | retains payload; fake demo auth; persists after confirmation |
| conflict | commit VERSION_CONFLICT / query state | StatusDialog | current generic close only; live reconciliation is future work |
| insufficient | commit INSUFFICIENT_QUANTITY | StatusDialog | close returns current form/list context |
| notfound | commit404 / query state | StatusDialog | presentation only; no current network recovery |
| timeout, loading, read, rate, session | query modal states / other mock error | StatusDialog variants | illustrative status actions; no live retry wiring |

List actions set `actionEntryId`; Detail uses `selectedId`. `modalEntry` resolves
actionEntryId before selectedId. `closeModal` clears both modal/actionEntryId.
History/delete/restore use selected, so a future new list action must establish
the appropriate selection rather than relying on a previous detail record.

## Add a navigation entry [D]

1. Declare view/action and expected owner/guard/empty/error state.
2. Add desktop sidebar and mobile dock in Shell; `onAdd` remains a distinct action.
3. Add App's initial query allowlist and render branch; decide selection precedence,
   filters/reset, close/back/cancel and post-command destination.
4. Reuse layout Grid/PageHeader and UI primitives; expose command callbacks.
5. Map live query/DTO through useExpiry/ApiClient and actual API/domain owner.
6. Verify desktop/mobile entry, direct initialization, detail/back, modal cancel,
   session failure, empty/filter states and keyboard behavior. If URL navigation
   is added, also verify Back/Forward and stale/deleted IDs.

No unseen route library is selected by this map; F-04 records that future decision.

## Breadcrumb versus routing

NAV-01 is implemented presentation on Detail only. Inventory/attention are the
usual parent containers; direct query/create from trash/settings retains that
View's label because existing onBack returns there. This is the collection/view
container, not a trail of every visited page. Current food remains one h1.
Narrow widths show nearest parent with a 40px back affordance; desktop ancestor
controls are 32px. Ancestors use callbacks because current App has no router.
No fake href, browser-history synchronization or live route is inferred.
Task outline: `.tmb/diagrams/README.md`; precise backlog: `.tmb/tasks/F-04/SPEC.md`.
</file>

