<file path=".tmb/responsive/PROBE-DISPOSITION.md">
# Supplied UI/UX probe — explicit disposition

Sources: `.tmb/evidence/responsive/probe-inventory/report.json` and
`.tmb/evidence/responsive/probe-detail/report.json`. Both57-step320…1440 sweeps
reported no broken width. Reports are kept raw, not edited to erase warnings.

| Finding | Evidence and disposition |
| --- | --- |
| Inventory P1/P2, detail P1: white text apparently on white/canvas | Probe's background-color traversal ignores opaque background-image gradients. CSS uses only accent/accent-hover endpoints; independent computed-color oracle measures normal6.46/5.03, hover5.03/6.46 and focus5.03 ratios against white. Original hover3.75 endpoint was actually corrected. Detector warning retained, not a real remaining selected contrast failure. |
| Focus rings flagged as a taste violation | UI/UX Pro Max visibly locatable keyboard focus wins over supporting UI skill's no-ring aesthetic. Intentional. Expanded traversal also caught and corrected breadcrumb-specific outline suppression; final checks validate actual visible focus/hit-test. |
| Border color changes on hover | Existing brand interaction feedback, stable1px width; no layout jump or command change. Retained presentation, not a responsive failure. |
| Repeated cards reach five text lines on desktop | Name/location/date/status/amount/actions are distinct required information. No clipping or duplicate copied rule established. Keep semantics rather than remove information to meet a taste count. |
| Centered content on1920px | Existing1180px content-width cap deliberately controls reading length; no hidden action or overflow. Retained brand layout, not unsupported production acceptance. |

React condensed review: direct primitive imports retained; no new fetch/auth/data
layer, dependency or inline component; controlled props/ISO date callbacks unchanged;
added visualViewport listeners have symmetric cleanup; portal bounds/focus remain
inside the existing lifecycle owners. Local fixture interception is only in ignored
test code and never exposed as product routes or sent to an API.
</file>

