# Plan: Expiry source-grounded context and feature navigation

Created: 2026-10-11. Milestone schedule, no invented deadline.
The human request authorizes map initialization, complete roadmap/navigator output,
reuse analysis and gitignore configuration in this turn. Stages1/2 of TMB planning
are performed together under that authorization. Product backlog items are proposals,
not authorization to change product behavior or apply DDL.

## 0. Decisions

| Topic | Source / options | Decision | Reason |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Target | active expiry checkout; hackathon plugin checkout | Map Expiry using hackathon TMB | User names hackathon as skill source; feature routes/API/DB/UI belong to current project |
| Current architecture | README API prose; web entry imports mockApi | Source entry wins for runtime map | Backend source presence does not prove web integration |
| Skill authority | 5 canonical src skills; extra Gemini/Bob extensions | Canonical workflows plus inspected navigator/audit semantics | Extension scripts src/roadmap.py/scaffold.py are absent |
| Context scale | full corpus versus small entry index | Root LAYOUT ≤3500 chars; small snapshots; six deep maps | Only load owners needed for the next task |
| Roadmap ownership | many subsystem boards | Root ROADMAP owns status; subsystem ROADMAP files are generated projections | Avoid a second hand-maintained status truth |
| Persistence truth | migrations, reference SQL, saved Workbench evidence | Definitions/runner separately from live schema | Auth002 source and approval comments are not evidence of application |
| Reuse | duplicate demo App; API/sandbox duplicate kernels | Classify exact clones versus intentional boundaries; proposed extraction tasks | Auth/public DTO/pool semantics make blind repository merge unsafe |
| Files in Git | source contracts/docs; task outputs | Exact root ignore rules plus .tmb/ | User requested local output exclusion, not ignoring tracked architecture docs |

## 1. Objectives

1. Find actual entrypoints, state/side-effect/lifecycle owners and dependencies.
2. Trace every visible view/action through UI, transport, API, logic, DB and feedback.
3. Catalog reusable UI/domain/repository interfaces with current consumers.
4. Provide feature-impact recipes and a status board per subsystem.
5. Enable repeatable context refresh, freshness checks and impact lookup.

Deliverables: root LAYOUT/PLAN/ROADMAP/AGENTS; .tmb layouts for web, api,
database, scan, contracts, delivery; navigation/flows/reuse/feature-impact maps;
source inventory with hashes/imports/routes/schema; navigator/verification report.

## 2. Technical design

Tracked source retains ownership of runtime/contracts/migrations. Local maps point
to those files and use [A] observed source, [C] inference, [D] proposal labels.
An in-memory demo chain and the implemented backend chain are described separately.
Local helper imports canonical TMB progress code and produces derived inventory,
context and subsystem status views. No empty src/db/src/ui folders are invented to
meet a scaffold rule: existing modules/features/migrations supply those roles.

## 4. Environments

| Profile | Purpose | Boundary |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| checkout / develop | source inspection and map validation | No production acceptance |
| installed local npm dependencies | targeted API checks and web type/build baseline | Tests can use injected repositories; MySQL integration is opt-in |
| local Python | scanner tests if required dependencies exist | Missing dependencies are reported, not auto-installed |
| browser / real DB / remote deployment | future feature-specific acceptance | Not required for generating the source map |

## 5. Schedule (10 milestones; product backlog remains separate)

### Phase 1: Source inventory
Build: root map, intent/status files and explicit ignore rules.
Measure: inspect entrypoints, migrations, imports, skill helpers and current Git state.
Write: reproducible hashes, branch/commit and skill availability evidence.
Exit criteria: source inventory exists; root index stays within3500 chars.

### Phase 2: Web navigation and reusable components
Build: web layout, complete view/action map and reuse interfaces.
Measure: static entry reachability and duplicate overlap.
Write: UI owners, transition/reset/return behavior and inactive integration components.
Exit criteria: every declared View/DetailAction and form mode is mapped to an owner.

### Phase 3: API, data, scan and delivery
Build: five additional subsystem maps and end-to-end flow descriptions.
Measure: router/contract endpoints, migrations/table definitions and domain ownership.
Write: schema relations, transaction rules, deployment wiring and contract gaps.
Exit criteria: every runtime route/table definition has a mapped source; live status remains bounded.

### Phase 4: Feature impact and reuse roadmap
Build: feature recipes plus subsystem roadmap projections linked to root IDs.
Measure: distinguish exact clones, shared variants and intentional separate adapters.
Write: source-backed findings, prioritized follow-up and invariants each change preserves.
Exit criteria: a feature request can identify navigation/UI/DTO/API/domain/DB/test owners.

### Phase 5: Navigator and verification
Build: repeatable progress/snapshot/impact/audit helper.
Measure: freshness/path/coverage/status/ignore checks; targeted existing checks where applicable.
Write: results and remaining runtime gaps in .tmb/VERIFICATION.md.
Exit criteria: generated outputs valid/ignored; compact context budget met; original tracked bytes preserved.

### Phase 6: Follow-up product work
Build: only the next explicitly requested feature/fix, using .tmb/maps/feature-impact.md.
Measure: checks at the actual boundaries changed, including browser/DB when relevant.
Write: update map/status/evidence after the change.
Exit criteria: each selected product task passes its recorded gate; unrequested backlog stays open.

## 6. Output outline

| Output | Producing phase |
| :--- | :--- |
| .tmb/evidence/source-inventory.json, root LAYOUT | Phase1 |
| web map, navigation, reuse, triage | Phase2 |
| api/database/scan/contracts/delivery maps, flows | Phase3 |
| feature-impact, findings, subsystem roadmaps | Phase4 |
| context snapshots, validator, verification | Phase5 |

## 7. Risks and fallbacks

| Risk | Evidence / signal | Fallback |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Existing document drift | README integration claim versus web import graph | Label current runtime and planned integration separately |
| Missing extension helpers | navigator/audit call files absent in hackathon | Small local helper under .tmb/tools; retain canonical progress algorithm |
| Duplicate kernels diverge | API pool differs from sandbox connection | Map owner boundaries before proposed extraction |
| Build/type baseline fails | Existing source may include stale imports | Record exact result and product backlog task; do not call map creation a feature fix |
| Context goes stale | captured source hash differs | audit fails; read affected source and update map, then refresh |
| Ignored outputs lost on another checkout | user requested gitignore | Copy local .tmb/root files deliberately; tracked source remains recoverable |

## 8. Deviations

- 2026-10-11: User explicitly authorized responsive UI completion with UI/UX Pro
  Max and typography guidance. Added Phase10 for source-owned presentation,
  small typing prerequisite, broad browser gates and map/status refresh; no
  backend/data/deployment expansion. Contract: `.tmb/responsive/PLAN.md`.

- 2026-10-11: User authorized a docs-grounded extension: Phase 7 adds docs/app
  layouts, task specs and linked local retrieval; Phase 8 adds reusable detail
  breadcrumbs. Existing source folders remain stable; local symlinks provide
  organized entrypoints. Product backlog Phase 6 remains separate and open.

### Phase 7: Docs-grounded context and specific task specs

- Build: classify documentation, create use-case/UML/navigation outlines, add
  docs/app layouts, feature specs, generated task boards and local symlink entries.
- Measure: verify target paths, source hashes, link diagnostics, FTS retrieval
  citations and all generated task projections against root status.
- Write: local reading order, namespace crosswalk, reorder receipt and search guide.
- Exit criteria: new local links resolve, indexes reject stale sources, each product
  task names requirements, owners, dependencies, acceptance and exclusions.

### Phase 8: Detail breadcrumb presentation

- Build: reuse Icon and existing CSS tokens in a controlled Breadcrumb component;
  Detail replaces its existing back presentation; both demo callers pass parent label.
- Measure: web build/type baseline plus local browser parent-return and width checks.
- Write: update web/navigation/reuse maps and bounded verification receipt.
- Exit criteria: detail parent labels match destination, returning preserves filters,
  no breadcrumb on top-level lists, no new router/API/DB owner.

### Phase 10: Responsive UI and typography

User explicitly authorized implementation on2026-10-11. Source contract and
independent gates are `.tmb/responsive/PLAN.md` and `.tmb/responsive/GATES.md`.
Build: shared text/focus/shell/reflow/modal/popover repairs; preserve brand/commands.
Measure: pages/forms,20px width sweep,200%CSS text, keyboard, reduced motion,
touch/contrast, compiled preview and before/after visual inspection.
Write: affected maps, root status/evidence and lexical context index.
Exit criteria: selected local responsive gates pass; no real-device/live approval inferred.

### Phase 9: Specific capability acceptance backlog

- Build: CAP-01…08 select manual capture, inventory/attention, detail/provenance,
  consume/discard, edit/recount, history, trash/restore and preferences as explicit
  vertical slices; DOC-01 and UX-01 scope existing source-link/UI warnings.
- Measure: each selected task's SPEC lists boundary-specific acceptance; live
  behavior cannot be closed by source maps, injected tests or demo checks alone.
- Write:18local task SPEC/ROADMAP pairs generated from the authored manifest;
  root status owns completion and preserves food/TMB/SYS/FINAL CHECK namespaces.
- Exit criteria: only subsequently selected product/hotfix work is implemented;
  current context request does not silently perform migrations/deployments.

- 2026-10-11: User explicitly requested complete initialization including roadmap;
  planner stage2 and local output publication are authorized in the same task.
- 2026-10-11: Missing extension engines replaced with a local context helper;
  existing monorepo owners are mapped instead of scaffolding another runtime tree.
