### Markdown document contract

Every major document must contain:

1. Document ID and title.
2. Purpose.
3. Status: Draft / Review / Approved / Blocked.
4. Evidence sources.
5. Definitions and assumptions.
6. Analysis or diagram.
7. Decisions and rationale.
8. Dependencies.
9. Open questions.
10. Links to related documents.
11. Verification criteria.

Use relative Markdown links.

Example:

`[Personas](../01-personas/README.md)`

All directories must have an index README.

The root README must provide an ordered reading path and show which documents are currently blocked by missing evidence.

Avoid copy-pasting the same business rule into multiple files. Link to the canonical rule instead.

