# 22. STAGE NINETEEN: TEST ARCHITECTURE

Testing must be embedded into the architecture, not postponed until deployment.

Define:

1. Unit tests for domain rules and pure functions.
2. Backend service tests.
3. API contract tests.
4. Database integration tests.
5. React component tests.
6. User-flow integration tests.
7. Python OCR tests.
8. Cross-service contract tests.
9. Authentication and authorization tests.
10. End-to-end tests.
11. Performance and reliability tests where necessary.
12. Accessibility checks.

Every important functional requirement must map to at least one appropriate test.

Test normal paths, invalid inputs, boundary cases, and recovery behavior.

Use deterministic test data when possible.

Use separate testing configuration and databases.

Do not rely exclusively on mocked database behavior to claim persistence correctness.

Define testing gates for pull requests and deployment.

